secubox-streamlit (1.4.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * streamlit-app@.service: move StartLimitIntervalSec=0 from [Service] to
    [Unit], where it belongs. Under [Service] systemd rejects the line
    outright ("Unknown key 'StartLimitIntervalSec' in section [Service],
    ignoring", logged at every instance start on the board) and the
    start-rate guard silently did nothing since #963 — the unit read as
    protected against an external `systemctl start` loop while nothing
    enforced it. Restart=no was unaffected. (ref #982)

